{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-41040","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72113","text":"Round 27, pass A.1 — P-7 closed, plus one you did not have"}]},{"id":"blk-41041","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72114","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pack:"},{"id":"spn-72115","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72116","marks":["code"],"text":"TRVM_R27A1_REVIEW_PACK.tar.gz"},{"id":"spn-72117","text":". Extract anywhere and run "},{"id":"spn-72118","marks":["code"],"text":"./verify.sh"},{"id":"spn-72119","text":". It replays 24 gates and "},{"id":"spn-72120","marks":["bold"],"text":"generates"},{"id":"spn-72121","text":" every number it prints; nothing in it transcribes a count. This run: "},{"id":"spn-72122","marks":["bold"],"text":"24 attempted / 24 passed / 0 failed / 0 skipped"},{"id":"spn-72123","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-41042","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72124","text":"1. P-7 reproduced first, then repaired"}]},{"id":"blk-41043","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72125","text":"I did not build against your report until I had the witness. Against the round-27A tree:"}]},{"id":"blk-41044","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"issued        request R → const(5)      psem-82eee05e…\nexecuted                   const(999)   psem-3b198d80…\nworker returned            999\naccept(fresh time-varying copy, that result)\n  → { ok:true, validated:true, fresh_at_check:true,\n      implementation_provenance:\"observed\", implementation_id:\"impl-js-derive-…\" }\naccept(FROZEN issued request, same result)\n  → result-program-mismatch"},{"id":"blk-41045","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72126","text":"Exactly as you described, including the part that makes it a forgery rather than luck: the only difference between the accepted and the refused case is the caller's retained ownership."}]},{"id":"blk-41046","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72127","marks":["bold"],"text":"Repaired"},{"id":"spn-72128","text":", and your diagnosis of "},{"id":"spn-72129","marks":["italic"],"text":"why"},{"id":"spn-72130","text":" was the useful part — the law was right and its reach was the constructor. "},{"id":"spn-72131","marks":["code"],"text":"derive_protocol.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72132","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72133","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.13.0"},{"id":"spn-72134","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-41047","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41049","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72135","text":"one exported "},{"id":"spn-72136","marks":["code"],"text":"ownCanonical()"},{"id":"spn-72137","text":" at the top of "},{"id":"spn-72138","marks":["code"],"text":"authorize"},{"id":"spn-72139","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72140","marks":["code"],"text":"wasIssued"},{"id":"spn-72141","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72142","marks":["code"],"text":"execute"},{"id":"spn-72143","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72144","marks":["code"],"text":"accept"},{"id":"spn-72145","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-41048","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41050","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72146","marks":["code"],"text":"observationOf"},{"id":"spn-72147","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72148","marks":["code"],"text":"ProgramRegistry.bind"}]},{"id":"blk-41051","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41053","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72149","marks":["code"],"text":"#issued"},{"id":"spn-72150","text":" keeps "},{"id":"spn-72151","marks":["code"],"text":"{request_sem_id, request}"},{"id":"spn-72152","text":" rather than the hash alone"}]}],"id":"blk-41052","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72153","marks":["code"],"text":"wasIssued"},{"id":"spn-72154","text":" returns the owned request; "},{"id":"spn-72155","marks":["code"],"text":"execute"},{"id":"spn-72156","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-72157","marks":["code"],"text":"accept"},{"id":"spn-72158","text":" read that"}]}],"id":"blk-41054","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72159","marks":["code"],"text":"res"},{"id":"spn-72160","text":" snapshotted once at "},{"id":"spn-72161","marks":["code"],"text":"accept"},{"id":"spn-72162","text":" entry; "},{"id":"spn-72163","marks":["code"],"text":"intent"},{"id":"spn-72164","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-72165","marks":["code"],"text":"options"},{"id":"spn-72166","text":" at "},{"id":"spn-72167","marks":["code"],"text":"authorize"},{"id":"spn-72168","text":" entry"}]}],"id":"blk-41056","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41058","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72169","text":"2. Where I did not take your preferred form, and why"}]},{"id":"blk-41059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72170","text":"You preferred "},{"id":"spn-72171","marks":["code"],"text":"execute(request_id)"},{"id":"spn-72172","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-72173","marks":["code"],"text":"accept(request_id, result)"},{"id":"spn-72174","text":", with the fallback of keeping the signature and using the stored object. "},{"id":"spn-72175","marks":["bold"],"text":"I took the fallback, and not for ergonomics."}]},{"id":"blk-41060","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72176","text":"An id is a "},{"id":"spn-72177","marks":["bold"],"text":"strictly weaker credential than the bytes."},{"id":"spn-72178","text":" Knowing the whole request implies knowing its "},{"id":"spn-72179","marks":["code"],"text":"request_id"},{"id":"spn-72180","text":"; the converse is false. "},{"id":"spn-72181","marks":["code"],"text":"execute(request_id)"},{"id":"spn-72182","text":" turns the id into a bearer token — anyone who has seen one can drive execution. Presenting the full request proves possession of every field, and "},{"id":"spn-72183","marks":["code"],"text":"wasIssued"},{"id":"spn-72184","text":" is what checks it."}]},{"id":"blk-41061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72185","text":"Keeping "},{"id":"spn-72186","marks":["code"],"text":"(req, res)"},{"id":"spn-72187","text":" gets "},{"id":"spn-72188","marks":["bold"],"text":"both"},{"id":"spn-72189","text":": full-bytes authentication "},{"id":"spn-72190","marks":["italic"],"text":"and"},{"id":"spn-72191","text":" owned exercise. The retained argument is now purely a claim to authenticate; nothing downstream reads it."}]},{"id":"blk-41062","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72192","text":"If you think the bearer-token concern is misplaced — e.g. because the request is handed to the caller anyway and confidentiality of "},{"id":"spn-72193","marks":["code"],"text":"request_id"},{"id":"spn-72194","text":" was never a property — say so and I will move to the stronger form. This is the one place I departed from your ruling."}]},{"id":"blk-41063","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72195","text":"3. P-7c — the same defect in the host, which your list did not reach"}]},{"id":"blk-41064","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72196","text":"Auditing the remaining entrypoints under the widened law found one more, and it is worse than P-7:"}]},{"id":"blk-41065","kind":"code","language":"js","text":"// ObservedExecutionHost.run(), v0.2.1\ninputCanonical = canonicalBytes(invocation)   // read 1 — the observation KEY\nrunNodeWorker(entry, invocation)              // read 2 — what actually RUNS"},{"id":"blk-41066","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72197","text":"An invocation honest on read 1 and hostile on read 2 is "},{"id":"spn-72198","marks":["bold"],"text":"keyed under one request and executed as another"},{"id":"spn-72199","text":". Measured:"}]},{"id":"blk-41067","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"reads of `message`: 2\nran -> 999 for program psem-3b198d800a9\nobservation under HONEST request bytes:        PRESENT\nobservation under the bytes that ACTUALLY ran: absent"},{"id":"blk-41068","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72200","text":"That is not \"a forged observation cannot be found\". It is a "},{"id":"spn-72201","marks":["bold"],"text":"true-looking observation for an execution that did not happen"},{"id":"spn-72202","text":", sitting in the table round 23 built so that relabelling would "},{"id":"spn-72203","marks":["italic"],"text":"move"},{"id":"spn-72204","text":" the key."}]},{"id":"blk-41069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72205","text":"It is unreachable through "},{"id":"spn-72206","marks":["code"],"text":"DerivationAuthority.execute"},{"id":"spn-72207","text":", whose invocation is assembled from owned parts. It is reachable by anything else holding a host — "},{"id":"spn-72208","marks":["code"],"text":"FilmAuthority"},{"id":"spn-72209","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-72210","marks":["code"],"text":"lowering_check"},{"id":"spn-72211","text":" both drive it directly — and the host is the only writer of the observation table. So the rule I applied:"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72212","marks":["bold"],"text":"The obligation belongs to the entrypoint, not to its politest caller."}]}],"id":"blk-41070","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-41072","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72213","marks":["code"],"text":"run()"},{"id":"spn-72214","text":" now launches the snapshot it keyed ("},{"id":"spn-72215","marks":["code"],"text":"JSON.parse(inputCanonical)"},{"id":"spn-72216","text":", zero extra reads). Host "},{"id":"spn-72217","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.3.0"},{"id":"spn-72218","text":". Frozen as P-7c in the same paired probe."}]},{"id":"blk-41073","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72219","text":"4. Enforcement is an enumeration, not three more witnesses"}]},{"id":"blk-41074","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72220","text":"Your point that the law had been applied where it was written down is the reason I did not just add cases. "},{"id":"spn-72221","marks":["code"],"text":"derive_realm_battery.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72222","text":" hands "},{"id":"spn-72223","marks":["bold"],"text":"every"},{"id":"spn-72224","text":" entrypoint a structurally identical argument whose every field counts its own reads, and fails past a one-read-per-field floor:"}]},{"id":"blk-41075","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"authorize/intent 7/7 · authorize/options 1/1 · wasIssued/req 11/11 · execute/req 11/11\naccept/req 11/11 · accept/res 18/18 · observationOf/req 11/11 · observationOf/res 18/18\nbindProgram/ast 2/2"},{"id":"blk-41076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72225","text":"Reintroducing the defect in "},{"id":"spn-72226","marks":["code"],"text":"execute"},{"id":"spn-72227","text":" alone → "},{"id":"spn-72228","marks":["bold"],"text":"`execute/req 33/11`"},{"id":"spn-72229","text":", and the case names the offender. A method added later with a live argument fails here with nobody remembering to come back."}]},{"id":"blk-41077","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72230","marks":["italic"],"text":"Falsification of my own instrument:"},{"id":"spn-72231","text":" the first version scored "},{"id":"spn-72232","marks":["code"],"text":"accept/res 0/0"},{"id":"spn-72233","text":" — the fixture under-granted, "},{"id":"spn-72234","marks":["code"],"text":"run.result"},{"id":"spn-72235","text":" was "},{"id":"spn-72236","marks":["code"],"text":"undefined"},{"id":"spn-72237","text":", and the result-side probes passed by measuring nothing. It now throws if the fixture does not execute and accept."}]},{"id":"blk-41078","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72238","text":"5. The stale diagnostic, and two more like it"}]},{"id":"blk-41079","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72239","text":"You flagged the "},{"id":"spn-72240","marks":["code"],"text":"derive_realm_battery.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72241","text":" \"Four rungs\" print. Fixed, and derived: "},{"id":"spn-72242","marks":["code"],"text":"SUPPLIER_LADDER"},{"id":"spn-72243","text":" is one frozen record in "},{"id":"spn-72244","marks":["code"],"text":"derive_protocol.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72245","text":", and every "},{"id":"spn-72246","marks":["bold"],"text":"live"},{"id":"spn-72247","text":" surface takes its count and wording from it. The frozen probes keep their own era's wording deliberately — each records the ladder as it stood when its witness was cut, and rewriting that would falsify a dated record."}]},{"id":"blk-41080","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72248","text":"Two others surfaced in the same pass:"}]},{"id":"blk-41081","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41083","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72249","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-72250","marks":["code"],"text":"derive_battery.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72251","text":"'s "},{"id":"spn-72252","marks":["code"],"text":"issuance-binds-the-whole-request"},{"id":"spn-72253","text":" had been calling the deleted"}]}],"id":"blk-41082","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41084","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72254","text":"three-argument "},{"id":"spn-72255","marks":["code"],"text":"accept(reg, req, res)"},{"id":"spn-72256","text":" since v0.10.0."},{"id":"spn-72257","marks":["bold"],"text":" `reg` landed in the `req` slot, `reg.request_id` was `undefined`, and the issuance table's miss on `undefined` produced the expected string `grant-not-issued-by-this-authority` "},{"id":"spn-72258","text":"by accident**. It asserted that string for eighteen rounds and never exercised the sentence it printed. Snapshot-at-entry is what surfaced it — a "},{"id":"spn-72259","marks":["code"],"text":"ProgramRegistry"},{"id":"spn-72260","text":" is not canonical data, so it now fails loudly instead of quietly agreeing. The "},{"id":"spn-72261","marks":["italic"],"text":"behaviour"},{"id":"spn-72262","text":" was always correct; only the instrument was wrong."}]},{"id":"blk-41085","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41087","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72263","text":"**"},{"id":"spn-72264","marks":["code"],"text":"observed_execution_host.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72265","text":" separated artifact-closure paths with a raw NUL byte in the"}]}],"id":"blk-41086","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-41088","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72266","text":"source.** "},{"id":"spn-72267","marks":["code"],"text":"file(1)"},{"id":"spn-72268","text":" classified the module as "},{"id":"spn-72269","marks":["code"],"text":"data"},{"id":"spn-72270","text":"; ugrep and every other text tool skipped it in silence. "},{"id":"spn-72271","marks":["italic"],"text":"A grep over that file returned nothing and read like an answer."},{"id":"spn-72272","text":" Now the "},{"id":"spn-72273","marks":["code"],"text":"\\u0000"},{"id":"spn-72274","text":" escape — identical string, visible module."}]},{"id":"blk-41089","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72275","text":"6. Gate"}]},{"id":"blk-41090","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72276","text":"grid "},{"id":"spn-72277","marks":["bold"],"text":"v1.30.0"},{"id":"spn-72278","text":" — 74 entries / 368 citations · "},{"id":"spn-72279","marks":["code"],"text":"derive_protocol.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72280","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72281","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.13.0"},{"id":"spn-72282","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-72283","marks":["code"],"text":"observed_execution_host.mjs"},{"id":"spn-72284","text":" "},{"id":"spn-72285","marks":["bold"],"text":"0.3.0"},{"id":"spn-72286","text":" · negative battery "},{"id":"spn-72287","marks":["bold"],"text":"182/182"},{"id":"spn-72288","text":" (eight new forgeries; three repointed off source text this round deleted) · bridge 48/48 · native film 16/16 · lowering refinement 9/9 film-evidenced · derive "},{"id":"spn-72289","marks":["bold"],"text":"45/45"},{"id":"spn-72290","text":" · realm "},{"id":"spn-72291","marks":["bold"],"text":"22/22"},{"id":"spn-72292","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-72293","marks":["bold"],"text":"twelve"},{"id":"spn-72294","text":" paired probes (newest: 3/3 frozen, 6/6 live) · harness 9/9 · runner 3/3 · review pack "},{"id":"spn-72295","marks":["bold"],"text":"24/24, 0 skipped"},{"id":"spn-72296","text":". "},{"id":"spn-72297","marks":["code"],"text":"scheduler_certificate.json"},{"id":"spn-72298","text":" byte-identical — "},{"id":"spn-72299","marks":["bold"],"text":"twenty-fourth"},{"id":"spn-72300","text":" consecutive round."}]},{"id":"blk-41091","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72301","text":"New law "},{"id":"spn-72302","marks":["code"],"text":"law:derivation.entry-snapshot@1"},{"id":"spn-72303","text":":"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72304","text":"Every authority operation consumes either an authority-owned object or one canonical snapshot made at entry. No trust decision authenticates one read of external state and exercises authority using another."}]}],"id":"blk-41092","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-41094","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72305","text":"7. Questions"}]},{"id":"blk-41095","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41097","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72306","marks":["bold"],"text":"The `execute(request_id)` disagreement"},{"id":"spn-72307","text":" (§2). Bearer-token concern valid, or is "},{"id":"spn-72308","marks":["code"],"text":"request_id"}]}],"id":"blk-41096","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-41098","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72309","text":"confidentiality a property TRVM never had and never wanted?"}]},{"id":"blk-41099","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72310","marks":["bold"],"text":"Scope statement I want ruled."},{"id":"spn-72311","text":" The module's free functions — "},{"id":"spn-72312","marks":["code"],"text":"deriveLocally"},{"id":"spn-72313","text":","}]}],"id":"blk-41100","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-41102","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72314","marks":["code"],"text":"validateForeignResult"},{"id":"spn-72315","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72316","marks":["code"],"text":"checkRequest"},{"id":"spn-72317","text":", "},{"id":"spn-72318","marks":["code"],"text":"checkIntent"},{"id":"spn-72319","text":" — do "},{"id":"spn-72320","marks":["bold"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-72321","text":" snapshot. The authority never passes them unowned data (verified: every call site now takes "},{"id":"spn-72322","marks":["code"],"text":"issued"},{"id":"spn-72323","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-72324","marks":["code"],"text":"ownRes"},{"id":"spn-72325","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-72326","marks":["code"],"text":"ownIntent"},{"id":"spn-72327","text":"). But they are exported, and a second authority built on them inherits the obligation without inheriting the mechanism. Is \"authority operations snapshot; free validators are pure functions over data the caller already owns\" the right line, or should the free functions carry it too? This is the most likely home of an @8."}]},{"id":"blk-41103","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-41105","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72328","marks":["bold"],"text":"Is the read-count enumeration the right terminating instrument"},{"id":"spn-72329","text":", or is there an argument class"}]}],"id":"blk-41104","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":3},{"id":"blk-41106","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72330","text":"it structurally cannot see? It counts property reads on a plain-object copy; a Proxy with an "},{"id":"spn-72331","marks":["code"],"text":"ownKeys"},{"id":"spn-72332","text":" trap is read once by "},{"id":"spn-72333","marks":["code"],"text":"canonicalBytes"},{"id":"spn-72334","text":" and I believe that is coherent, but I would rather you attacked it than that I asserted it."}]},{"id":"blk-41107","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-72335","text":"8. Pass B — your rulings taken as given"}]},{"id":"blk-41108","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72336","text":"Recorded in "},{"id":"spn-72337","marks":["code"],"text":"governance/round-11-ledger.md"},{"id":"spn-72338","text":" items 166–167, not to be re-litigated: separate "},{"id":"spn-72339","marks":["code"],"text":"instantiation_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-72340","text":" with its own law; the relation-not-invocation split against "},{"id":"spn-72341","marks":["code"],"text":"inputs_sem_id"},{"id":"spn-72342","text":"; the "},{"id":"spn-72343","marks":["code"],"text":"InstantiationReceipt"},{"id":"spn-72344","text":" verified by independent re-instantiation, no film; I-4 as the inverse of round 16 with "},{"id":"spn-72345","marks":["code"],"text":"input-port(\"x\")"},{"id":"spn-72346","text":" at the canonical target-AST layer and "},{"id":"spn-72347","marks":["bold"],"text":"no Unicode normalization"},{"id":"spn-72348","text":" of source input strings; the three falsifiers rather than one; Fixture A "},{"id":"spn-72349","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-72350","text":" and Fixture B a purpose-built DUP-ERA witness."}]},{"id":"blk-41109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-72351","text":"Posture change accepted: no more proactive P-hunting. Next is the inputs decision record, then the "},{"id":"spn-72352","marks":["code"],"text":"church_exp_2_2"},{"id":"spn-72353","text":" DUP film."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaierawolr5rkcjazck6tbqp6c32do2k6ssikksiyjlyupfrjjkrsrwqya","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}